NAME
====

**wattle-apps** - manage installed applications

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle apps** _verb_ [_argument_]

DESCRIPTION
===========

Manage the applications installed under ``*prefix*``. Modules are installed in
``lib/wattle``, programs in ``bin`` and man pages in ``share/man`` under it.
A build made without the OS library does not include ***apps***, and each verb
exits with status 1 after saying so. **a** is a synonym for ***apps***.

VERBS
=====

- ***install*** [_source_ [_ref_]]:
  Install an application. _source_ is a directory, a name ending in ``.tar`` or
  ``.tar.gz``, or a Git repository. A directory is installed as it is. A name
  ending in ``.tar`` or ``.tar.gz`` is downloaded with **curl** and unpacked
  with **tar**. Anything else is cloned with **git**. With no _source_, the
  current directory is installed. If the application contains ``pkg.wattle`` or
  ``pkg/init.wattle``, ***apps*** runs the hooks of that script and nothing
  else. Otherwise ***apps*** builds each ``:exe`` artifact of ``info.edn`` with
  ***build*** ***exe***, installs the program in ``bin``, and installs each
  file in the ``:man`` vector of ``info.edn`` in ``share/man``. The section is
  the digit that ends the file name, so ``man/greet.1`` is installed in
  ``man1``. A ``:web`` artifact is not installed, and an application with a
  ``:lib`` artifact needs a script. _ref_ is a branch or tag, and applies only
  to a Git repository.

- ***upgrade*** [_name_]:
  Install the application _name_ again from the source it was installed from.
  An application installed from a tarball or a Git repository is downloaded
  again. With no _name_, every installed application is upgraded.

- ***remove*** _name_:
  Remove the application _name_.

- ***list***:
  List the installed applications.

EXAMPLES
========

Install applications from a directory, a tarball and a Git repository, and list
the installed applications:

````
$ wattle apps install ./my-app
$ wattle apps install https://example.com/my-app.tar.gz
$ wattle apps install https://example.com/my-app.git v1.2
$ wattle apps list
````

Install every application again from its source, and remove one:

````
$ wattle apps upgrade
$ wattle apps remove my-app
````

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`, `wattle-build(1)`, `wattle-deps(1)`, `wattle-applications(7)`
